for each of the two actual lattices. lambda=coord_0:A->S
is S-linear and lambda|S=id. Retain frame_theorem.1.1
(relation preservation on valueFieldPoints fracSpan) and
span_kisinLoc (M=A N). Since N lies in those valueFieldPoints,
for any two finite expressions of x in M, subtracting their
expressions gives sum a_j n_j=0, hence sum lambda(a_j)n_j=0.
Thus R_N(x)=sum lambda(a_j)n_j is well-defined, S-linear, and
R_N(n)=n for n in N. For any native equivariant lattice map F,
F(N) subset N', so F R_N(x)=sum lambda(a_j)F(n_j)=R_N' F(x).
This gives exists_coordRetract and Hom.map_coordRetract.
In particular R commutes with the coefficient-root multiplication
used in the definition of the letter eigenspace; it fixes that
letter because the eigenvalue letterTeich i belongs to S.

